  "_comment": "Inputs for build_panoramas.py: one NASA Photojournal 360-degree mosaic per stop. Every field here is catalogue metadata from the PIA page. Position, elevation and heading come from shared/poses/<site>_poses.csv; walkability, slope and relay passes come from the pipeline's own grid and pass bundles. The official caption is fetched from `page` at build time. hfov_deg is the horizontal span of the mosaic; center_heading_deg is the compass bearing of its centre column, set only when the official caption states it (PIA20840: 'North is at both ends and south is in the center', so 180); null: the rover's yaw at that sol, because the mosaic's own pointing is not published with the JPEG. sol_end marks a mosaic taken over several sols at one parked position.",
